    {
      "id": "6f5c9e09ffe9b5a64365b53ba034a64e4cb4c195",
      "individual_note": true,
      "resolvable": false,
      "notes": [
        {
          "id": 1666470700,
          "type": null,
          "body": "1. Does this mean that if somebody's set the size in any profile, so that size is stored in that profile's recent file, that size will not be used if main-branch (and, ultimately, 4.4.x/5.0.x/whatever the main branch becomes) Wireshark, causing Wireshark to show up in the default size?\n2. If different profiles have different layouts, could that cause a user to want different sizes in different profiles, e.g. a wider window with side-to-side panes and a taller window with vertically-stacked panes?",
          "author": {
            "id": 5636682,
            "username": "guyharris",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "Guy Harris",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
            "avatar_url": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/1b7c243a9b1d6587a9a9067e5d83aba1e87212df7c4eeae3690f791ecbe4675a?s=80&d=identicon",
            "web_url": "https://gitlab.com/guyharris"
          },
          "created_at": "2023-11-25T20:05:06.767Z",
          "updated_at": "2023-11-25T20:05:06.767Z",
          "system": false,
          "noteable_id": 265880268,
          "noteable_type": "MergeRequest",
          "project_id": 7898047,
          "resolvable": false,
          "confidential": false,
          "internal": false,
          "imported": false,
          "imported_from": "none",
          "noteable_iid": 13443,
          "commands_changes": {}
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "aade5b83f6ec0176d1e1dc477afe81e498c8bdca",
      "individual_note": false,
      "resolvable": true,
      "resolved": false,
      "notes": [
        {
          "id": 1666518494,
          "type": "DiscussionNote",
          "body": "> Does this mean that if somebody's set the size in any profile\n\nThe size has long (for fifteen years) been stored in recent_common. I recently added using `saveGeometry` for the main window as well as the older GTK-based window calculations, but it's only currently used when the window was maximized, because it tracks on which monitor a window was maximized, and what the un-maximized size was, which our old method doesn't do. I initially added it in recent instead of recent_common like the other main window geometry settings.\n\nIf the new method is unavailable, the old method is used, which should be fine for people switching back and forth between 4.4 and earlier, since 4.4 continues to write the old settings, and read the old settings as a fallback.\n\n> If different profiles have different layouts, could that cause a user to want different sizes in different profiles, e.g. a wider window with side-to-side panes and a taller window with vertically-stacked panes?\n\nYes, absolutely. That is a good reason to consider moving the main window geometry from recent_common to recent, but it would make sense to move all the main window geometry settings to per profile at once I think.\n\nThe per profile recent settings store the splitter / pane information but not the overall geometry.",
          "author": {
            "id": 6764551,
            "username": "johnthacker",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "John Thacker",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
            "avatar_url": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/99c30adacedf45514aaf711ba8a44f56322ebb53e9b550b7e3c9cd83bd6a1408?s=80&d=identicon",
            "web_url": "https://gitlab.com/johnthacker"
          },
          "created_at": "2023-11-25T22:03:52.622Z",
          "updated_at": "2023-11-25T22:14:27.333Z",
          "system": false,
          "noteable_id": 265880268,
          "noteable_type": "MergeRequest",
          "project_id": 7898047,
          "resolvable": true,
          "resolved": false,
          "resolved_by": null,
          "resolved_at": null,
          "confidential": false,
          "internal": false,
          "imported": false,
          "imported_from": "none",
          "noteable_iid": 13443,
          "commands_changes": {}
        },
        {
          "id": 1666520895,
          "type": "DiscussionNote",
          "body": "The design has always been to have the window size, position and maximised state common for all profiles. I don't want any window to resize when switching profiles, and I want the current design to continue.\n\nI want splitters / pane sizes and layout to be profile specific because of different use cases.",
          "author": {
            "id": 4753670,
            "username": "stigbjorlykke",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "Stig Bjørlykke",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
            "avatar_url": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/905aafc6b50e246885f5ea9273a9dc4f22e2658b71f9a1b551b797082bec3f80?s=80&d=identicon",
            "web_url": "https://gitlab.com/stigbjorlykke"
          },
          "created_at": "2023-11-25T22:14:27.288Z",
          "updated_at": "2023-11-25T22:14:27.288Z",
          "system": false,
          "noteable_id": 265880268,
          "noteable_type": "MergeRequest",
          "project_id": 7898047,
          "resolvable": true,
          "resolved": false,
          "resolved_by": null,
          "resolved_at": null,
          "confidential": false,
          "internal": false,
          "imported": false,
          "imported_from": "none",
          "noteable_iid": 13443,
          "commands_changes": {}
        },
        {
          "id": 1666521516,
          "type": "DiscussionNote",
          "body": "> I want splitters / pane sizes and layout to be profile specific because of different use cases.\n\nSo people would manually resize the window if changes to pane sizes or layout, as a result of a profile changes, result in a window that's too wide/not wide enough or too tall/not tall enough?",
          "author": {
            "id": 5636682,
            "username": "guyharris",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "Guy Harris",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
            "avatar_url": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/1b7c243a9b1d6587a9a9067e5d83aba1e87212df7c4eeae3690f791ecbe4675a?s=80&d=identicon",
            "web_url": "https://gitlab.com/guyharris"
          },
          "created_at": "2023-11-25T22:17:20.586Z",
          "updated_at": "2023-11-25T22:17:20.586Z",
          "system": false,
          "noteable_id": 265880268,
